          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>This forest is the canonical statement layer of the
finite-field-invariants project: definitions, theorems, conjectures, and
the dependency skeleton that links them — kept separate from the
narrative journal (notes/steenrod-hsop.tex) and the experiment record
(experiments/). Notation is fixed here; when the journal and the forest
disagree, the forest wins and the journal gets patched.</html:p>
            <html:p>Each statement lives at a permanent numeric address. The number means
nothing and never changes: nodes are renamed, restated, split and
refuted, and the address survives all of it, so a citation written today
still resolves after the mathematics moves. The readable concordance is
ADDRESSES.md, regenerated by every build.</html:p>
