      <fr:mainmatter>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0021/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0021</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0021/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="(M8): the per-cell modality reduction at n = 8">(M8): the per-cell modality reduction at n = 8</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">height</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">conditional</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>(M8). Every cell of the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 8]]></fr:tex> address decomposition has
per-cell modality small enough that no cell can carry a violation of
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*)</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> Two ingredients. <html:strong>Pseudo-Levi collapse</html:strong>: the per-cell
modality satisfies <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[M(8) = 1]]></fr:tex>, so each cell is a one-modulus problem of
the kind <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0020/" title="Height at n ≤ 7" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0020/" display-uri="ffi-0020" type="local">height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  7]]></fr:tex></fr:link> already handles.
<html:strong>Torus-defect dichotomy</html:strong>: a cell either has torus defect placing
it below the threshold, or lies in the gap-7 regime where Lang--Weil
against <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[4v^9]]></fr:tex> excludes it. The two cases are exhaustive.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> Proven by theory, conditional only on the published GMR2014 data
for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A_7]]></fr:tex> (degree 9, leading coefficient 4). The genericity step in
pseudo_levi_gap.sage needs <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[|F| \gtrsim  10^4]]></fr:tex> to be visible
numerically; the argument itself is characteristic-free.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0027/" title="Borel modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0027/" display-uri="ffi-0027" type="local">Borel modality</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0028/" title="U-modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0028/" display-uri="ffi-0028" type="local">U-modality</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: journal thm:m8 (sixteenth pass); pseudo_levi_gap.sage
all-pass; commit afdac1f.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0023/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0023</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0023/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="(S): the n = 9 reduction">(S): the n = 9 reduction</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">height</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>(S). At <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 9]]></fr:tex> the violation locus of <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*)</fr:link> is
covered by finitely many identified loci, all of which are cold.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> Three layers, all machine-checked. <html:strong>Sweep census by
involutions</html:strong>: 2620 classes, of which the three <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f = 3]]></fr:tex> classes are
exactly the three maximizer tableaux (verified) and 51 carry <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f = 2]]></fr:tex>.
<html:strong>Linear layer</html:strong>: 4862 ideals across 5 characteristics, all cold,
including exact <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathbb {Q}]]></fr:tex>; a covering theorem makes the finite check
exhaustive. <html:strong>Cascade</html:strong>: 53 safe ten-moduli loci, with the boundary
probe at layer 1 also cold.</html:p>
            <html:p>The captured <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f = 2]]></fr:tex> case is killed characteristic-free by the
cross-term and tangent lemmas, and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\operatorname {mod}(B : \mathfrak {n}_{9}) = 3]]></fr:tex> characteristic-free,
so no <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f = 3]]></fr:tex> violation is available either. The residual ledger is
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[72 = 53 + \sum  c'_i + m_{\text {unknown}}]]></fr:tex>, closed by
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0024/" title="(S+): the ledger conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0024/" display-uri="ffi-0024" type="local">(S+)</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0027/" title="Borel modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0027/" display-uri="ffi-0027" type="local">Borel modality</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: journal subsec:seventeenth and subsec:eighteenth;
census53_cells.log (canonical, 53 addresses degree 10 lc 1 per
characteristic), sweep16_rank.log (exact-<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathbb {Q}]]></fr:tex> ranks, 16
nonlinear loci); commit e8c7430.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0024/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0024</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0024/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="(S+): the ledger conjecture">(S+): the ledger conjecture</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>conjecture</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">height</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>(S+). In the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 9]]></fr:tex> ledger
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[72 = 53 + \sum  c'_i + m_{\text {unknown}}]]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \sum  c'_i = 19 \iff  m_{\text {unknown}} = 0,
]]></fr:tex>
and either side implies <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0023/" title="(S): the n = 9 reduction" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0023/" display-uri="ffi-0023" type="local">(S)</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> Stated as a conjecture during the seventeenth pass and
discharged in the eighteenth: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c' = [5, 7, 7]]]></fr:tex>, so <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\sum  c'_i = 19]]></fr:tex>
and the unknown count is zero. Kept as its own node because it is the
hinge the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 9]]></fr:tex> argument turns on, and because a <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 10]]></fr:tex> analogue
is the natural next ledger.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0023/" title="(S): the n = 9 reduction" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0023/" display-uri="ffi-0023" type="local">(S): the n = 9 reduction</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: journal subsec:seventeenth (statement), subsec:eighteenth
(discharge); the jtype truncation bug found and fixed en route; commit
e8c7430.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0022/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0022</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0022/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Height at n = 8">Height at n = 8</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>corollary</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">height</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">conditional</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">The height conjecture</fr:link> holds for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 8]]></fr:tex> and every prime
power <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>, conditional only on the published GMR2014 <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A_7]]></fr:tex> row.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> The address reduction turns <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*)</fr:link> at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 8]]></fr:tex>
into a per-cell statement, and <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0021/" title="(M8): the per-cell modality reduction at n = 8" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0021/" display-uri="ffi-0021" type="local">(M8)</fr:link> discharges every
cell. The two-moduli locus is exactly the four O4 ideals, which are
Steinberg slices of involutions and therefore safe,
characteristic-free.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">The height conjecture</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0021/" title="(M8): the per-cell modality reduction at n = 8" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0021/" display-uri="ffi-0021" type="local">(M8): the per-cell modality reduction at n = 8</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: journal cor:height-n8 (fifteenth and sixteenth passes);
commit afdac1f.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0025/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0025</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0025/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Height at n = 9">Height at n = 9</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>corollary</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">height</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">conditional</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">The height conjecture</fr:link> holds for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 9]]></fr:tex> and every prime
power <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>, conditional on the published <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A_7]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A_8]]></fr:tex> modality rows
and on the machine certificates below.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0023/" title="(S): the n = 9 reduction" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0023/" display-uri="ffi-0023" type="local">(S)</fr:link> covers the violation locus and
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0024/" title="(S+): the ledger conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0024/" display-uri="ffi-0024" type="local">(S+)</fr:link> closes its ledger; the three maximizers have
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\operatorname {lc} = 3]]></fr:tex> and are safe, so no violation survives. Exact address
polynomials come from the GR cell engine.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">The height conjecture</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0023/" title="(S): the n = 9 reduction" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0023/" display-uri="ffi-0023" type="local">(S): the n = 9 reduction</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0024/" title="(S+): the ledger conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0024/" display-uri="ffi-0024" type="local">(S+): the ledger conjecture</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: journal cor:height-n9 (eighteenth pass); census53_cells.log,
sweep16_rank.log; commit e8c7430.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0019/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0019</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0019/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Height at n ≤ 5">Height at n ≤ 5</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">height</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">The height conjecture</fr:link> holds for every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  5]]></fr:tex> and
every prime power <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> For <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  5]]></fr:tex> the Borel has finitely many orbits on the
nilradical (Kashiarov; Hille--Röhrle), so <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*)</fr:link> is not
needed: the isotropy bound of <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0014/" title="Orbital varieties are Lagrangian" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0014/" display-uri="ffi-0014" type="local">the orbital-variety theorem</fr:link>,
plus at most one modulus of orbits, covers every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[B]]></fr:tex>-stable
irreducible subvariety.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">The height conjecture</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0014/" title="Orbital varieties are Lagrangian" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0014/" display-uri="ffi-0014" type="local">Orbital varieties are Lagrangian</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: journal sec:small-n; Kashiarov, Hille--Röhrle for the
finiteness input.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0020/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0020</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0020/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Height at n ≤ 7">Height at n ≤ 7</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">height</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">The height conjecture</fr:link> holds for every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  7]]></fr:tex> and
every prime power <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>, unconditionally.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> The modality theorem: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\operatorname {mod}(B : \mathfrak {n}_{n}) = 1]]></fr:tex> for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 6, 7]]></fr:tex>. With
at most one modulus of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[B]]></fr:tex>-orbits on the nilradical, the
two-moduli case of <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*)</fr:link> never arises, so
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0014/" title="Orbital varieties are Lagrangian" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0014/" display-uri="ffi-0014" type="local">the orbital-variety theorem</fr:link> closes every subvariety. The
modality inputs are published rows discharged against machine
certificates (Goddard--Goodwin; GMR2).</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">The height conjecture</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0014/" title="Orbital varieties are Lagrangian" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0014/" display-uri="ffi-0014" type="local">Orbital varieties are Lagrangian</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0027/" title="Borel modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0027/" display-uri="ffi-0027" type="local">Borel modality</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: journal thm:height-n7 (fourteenth pass); census 275/276/277
plus the diamond; verified against Goddard--Goodwin and GMR2.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0018/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0018</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0018/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Height at n ≤ 9">Height at n ≤ 9</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">height</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">conditional</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">The height conjecture</fr:link> holds for every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  9]]></fr:tex> and
every prime power <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>. Unconditionally for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  7]]></fr:tex>; for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 8, 9]]></fr:tex>
conditional on published modality rows and machine certificates.</html:p>
            <html:p>The ladder is climbed rung by rung, because <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*)</fr:link> is
unavailable and each <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex> has to be discharged by its own count. The
rungs are <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0019/" title="Height at n ≤ 5" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0019/" display-uri="ffi-0019" type="local">height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  5]]></fr:tex></fr:link>,
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0020/" title="Height at n ≤ 7" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0020/" display-uri="ffi-0020" type="local">height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  7]]></fr:tex></fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0022/" title="Height at n = 8" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0022/" display-uri="ffi-0022" type="local">height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 8]]></fr:tex></fr:link> and
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0025/" title="Height at n = 9" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0025/" display-uri="ffi-0025" type="local">height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 9]]></fr:tex></fr:link>; their conditionality differs and is
stated on each.</html:p>
